<section class="legal-section" id="terms-2">
    <h2>2. The service</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Wesal is a digital marriage-introduction platform. It allows members to create a profile, search for other members and communicate with them inside the application. Some services are free and others are paid, as described in section 5.</li>
        <li>The service is intended only for people aged 18 or over who are seeking a serious marriage, for personal purposes only.</li>
        <li>We do not guarantee that you will find a partner, receive a particular number of suggestions, messages or profile views, obtain another person's consent, establish a successful relationship or get married. Search results depend on decisions made by other people, which we do not control.</li>
        <li>We do not verify the identity of every member or the accuracy of everything they write, such as their age, marital status or intentions. Each member is responsible for their own information. Verify information independently before making personal decisions or arranging a meeting.</li>
        <li>Meetings, relationships and agreements between members outside the application are not part of our service. We are not a party to them.</li>
        <li>Wesal does not provide legal advice, immigration or residence services, visa services or marriage solemnisation.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section class="legal-section" id="terms-3">
    <h2>3. Registration and accounts</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Registration is available to natural persons aged 18 or over. By registering, you confirm that you are at least 18 and are seeking a serious marriage.</li>
        <li>Each person may have only one account. Accounts may not be transferred or sold.</li>
        <li>Enter accurate information and update it when it changes. Photos uploaded to your profile must be photos of you.</li>
        <li>Keep your login details confidential and notify us immediately if you suspect that someone else has accessed your account.</li>
        <li>You have no automatic right to enter into a contract with us. We may refuse registration for an objective reason, such as reasonable doubts about a person's age, a duplicate account or a previously blocked account.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

