<section class="legal-section" id="terms-10">
    <h2>10. Reports, content review and blocking</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Point of contact (Articles 11 and 12 DSA):</strong> Users and public authorities may contact us at <a href="mailto:wesalsyrien@gmail.com">wesalsyrien@gmail.com</a>. Available languages: German, Arabic and English.</li>
        <li><strong>Reporting:</strong> Anyone may report content or an account using the “Report” button inside the application or by email, providing a clear reason. We confirm receipt and notify the reporting person of the decision (Article 16 DSA). You may also block a member from their profile. A blocked member can no longer see or message you.</li>
        <li><strong>How we review:</strong> A member of our team reviews reports. We do not read private messages except for the material submitted by the reporting person.</li>
        <li><strong>Measures:</strong> Depending on the seriousness of the violation, we may issue a warning, remove content, temporarily hide a profile, temporarily suspend an account or terminate the contract. We consider legitimate interests and proportionality.</li>
        <li><strong>Serious violations that may justify immediate termination:</strong> being under 18, fraud or requests for money, threats or blackmail, sexual content, impersonation, commercial exploitation, or repeated violations after a warning.</li>
        <li><strong>Statement of reasons (Article 17 DSA):</strong> We notify you of restrictions on your account or content, including the reason and the rule that was breached, unless the law prevents us or the content is manifestly commercial spam.</li>
        <li><strong>Appeal:</strong> You may challenge a decision by emailing <a href="mailto:wesalsyrien@gmail.com">wesalsyrien@gmail.com</a> within six months. Where possible, a person who did not make the original decision reviews the appeal. Your right to bring a matter before a court remains unaffected.</li>
        <li>We notify the authorities if we suspect a criminal offence involving a threat to a person's life or safety (Article 18 DSA).</li>
    </ol>
</section>

